1
00:00:58,016 --> 00:01:00,060
I've never once been
late for an appointment

2
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:01,603
in all this time.

3
00:01:01,686 --> 00:01:03,313
It's one of my cardinal rules.

4
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:04,898
But

5
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:07,776
the traffic is especially bad today.
We haven't moved at all.

6
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:49,109
'Golden Best, Vol. 1'

7
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:53,530
'A Side'

8
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:54,948
Cut! Okay!

9
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:05,959
All right, Ms. Oh Young-ran has wrapped
her final scene today!

10
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:08,586
Great work!

11
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:09,712
Great work!

12
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,297
You worked so hard,
Ms. Oh!

13
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:12,966
Great work.

14
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:19,931
Today's appointment
is Young-ran.

15
00:02:20,014 --> 00:02:21,683
She's an actress.

16
00:02:21,766 --> 00:02:24,144
She used to appear in
lots of cosmetics ads

17
00:02:24,227 --> 00:02:27,021
and often played the lead
in TV dramas.

18
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:33,153
It was a close call,

19
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:36,030
but thankfully, I still made
to her appointment on time.

20
00:02:40,743 --> 00:02:43,288
I'm going to miss you so much, Ms. Oh.

21
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:45,123
You should've appreciated me
while I was here, you brats.

22
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:48,960
I'll take the rest off at home.

23
00:02:49,043 --> 00:02:50,378
Sure, Ms. Oh. Go ahead.

24
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:51,462
All right. Great work, everyone.

25
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:53,548
You worked so hard, Ms. Oh.

26
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:54,924
- You should take this with you.
- Huh?

27
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:56,551
Thanks.

28
00:02:58,344 --> 00:03:00,430
- See you again.
- Yes, Ms. Oh.

29
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:02,348
Go home and get some rest.

30
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:03,516
Goodbye.

31
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:10,398
Oh, goodness. Honestly,
what was I thinking?

32
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:12,150
This perfume is brand-new!

33
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:13,484
I left it behind.

34
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:17,780
My dear kids worked so hard, didn't you?

35
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:19,282
Yes.

36
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:23,369
Now that we won't have to deal with Oh Young-ran
anymore, let's get back to work with a smile!

37
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:25,038
Yes!

38
00:03:25,121 --> 00:03:26,497
No, no.

39
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:28,750
She keeps telling me how she was the lead
in a drama when I was three

40
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,418
and I don't know why she
brings it up all the time.

41
00:03:30,501 --> 00:03:31,336
Exactly.

42
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:32,670
How am I supposed to know about a drama
my own mom hasn't even watched?

43
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:34,923
Exactly.

44
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:37,383
Still wanting to be treated
like the star...

45
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:38,843
It's kind of sad.

46
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:42,555
You did swear the most.

47
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,724
When did I ever, senior?

48
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:46,559
- I don't know. Sort it out.
- Yes.

49
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,691
Here you go.

50
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:54,651
Did filming go well?

51
00:03:54,734 --> 00:03:57,946
I really can't work with these people.

52
00:03:58,029 --> 00:04:00,907
They hand me a rewritten script
on the day of the shoot...

53
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:03,159
and tell me I'm dying today.

54
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:06,120
They had a little disagreement
with the writer...

55
00:04:06,704 --> 00:04:08,581
and they kill off the character?

56
00:04:09,207 --> 00:04:12,502
Shouldn't the show come before
personal feelings?

57
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:15,129
Isn't that right, driver?

58
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:17,340
Yes.

59
00:04:17,423 --> 00:04:18,424
As for me,

60
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:21,803
I'm no expert on acting,
so I can't say for sure,

61
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:25,622
but I do think it's best to keep
work and personal matters separate.

62
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:27,267
Let's go.

63
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:47,328
Driver,

64
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:50,206
please play my go-to song.

65
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:53,793
Did you know the term 'go-to song'

66
00:04:53,876 --> 00:04:57,422
comes from Japanese kabuki?

67
00:04:58,089 --> 00:05:01,009
A Japanese actor named
Ichikawa Danjūrō

68
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:03,761
selected 18 kabuki plays

69
00:05:03,845 --> 00:05:06,306
- and announced them...
- Driver, just...

70
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:08,641
Please play my number-one song.

71
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:11,477
Sure.

72
00:05:29,787 --> 00:05:30,872
♪ Tonight ♪

73
00:05:32,498 --> 00:05:35,001
♪ Somehow, I feel you'll ♪

74
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:43,468
♪ Come back to my side ♪

75
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:46,679
♪ You ♪

76
00:05:48,097 --> 00:05:50,349
♪ Have gone away ♪

77
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:58,483
♪ I don't regret it now ♪

78
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:02,278
♪ It's just ♪

79
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:06,365
♪ The years gone by ♪

80
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:14,957
♪ Feel like falling rain ♪

81
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:20,755
♪ But when you suddenly ♪

82
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:24,050
♪ Come to mind ♪

83
00:06:24,842 --> 00:06:29,847
♪ This heart will ache again ♪

84
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:33,601
It hurts.

85
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:39,607
♪ Time passes, and we forget ♪

86
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:41,651
♪ But love ♪

87
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:45,530
♪ Is like rain on the window ♪

88
00:06:47,865 --> 00:06:49,575
♪ But love ♪

89
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:53,621
♪ Is like rain on the window ♪

90
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:57,375
♪ Love, love ♪

91
00:06:57,458 --> 00:07:01,504
♪ Is like rain on the window ♪

92
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,101
Driver.

93
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:19,272
Want to come in for ramen?

94
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:21,524
Pardon?

95
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:25,945
Aren't you hungry?

96
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:29,532
Yes.

97
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:38,624
A long time ago,

98
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:41,502
this was where my first scandal broke.

99
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:44,964
Now I can eat ramen with my
driver right out in the open,

100
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:47,967
and nobody cares.

101
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:53,931
- Oh, right. Driver.
- Yes?

102
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:56,392
Would you mind watching something with me?

103
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:57,518
Sure.

104
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:59,645
This drama's ratings have
been through the roof.

105
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:00,730
Yes, yes.

106
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:03,024
Just watch the parts I'm in...

107
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:04,192
- Yes.
- Yes.

108
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:08,112
Why is there salt

109
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:09,405
in my house?

110
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:11,282
I'm sorry, ma'am.

111
00:08:13,826 --> 00:08:14,911
I

112
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:19,332
told you not to put salt in
the side dishes for the child.

113
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:21,834
Didn't I?

114
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:25,254
I really didn't, ma'am.

115
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:26,881
It came free

116
00:08:26,964 --> 00:08:30,510
with the soy sauce.
It seemed a shame to throw it away.

117
00:08:37,266 --> 00:08:39,310
You'd have to be pickled in salt

118
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:42,438
to learn how dangerous sodium is, right?

119
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:54,784
At this point,

120
00:08:54,867 --> 00:08:56,827
I got so caught up in the role

121
00:08:56,911 --> 00:09:00,081
that I was still angry
even after filming ended.

122
00:09:00,164 --> 00:09:01,832
For days, if my food tasted salty,

123
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:03,292
I'd just keep

124
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:05,753
getting so angry.

125
00:09:06,504 --> 00:09:09,257
So I had no choice but to eat
salt-free food for a few days.

126
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:10,925
All of a sudden today, hey...

127
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:14,303
I'm really craving ramen. Ha ha.

128
00:09:18,015 --> 00:09:19,976
Oh, I think they recognize me.

129
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:22,270
Driver, could I borrow your hat?

130
00:09:22,853 --> 00:09:25,648
Well, m-my hat doesn't have a brim...

131
00:09:27,483 --> 00:09:28,776
I don't have anything on my face, do I?

132
00:09:30,695 --> 00:09:31,529
Hello.

133
00:09:32,488 --> 00:09:35,032
I've taken my makeup off, so...

134
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:35,950
Oh, okay.

135
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:37,702
Maybe we can take a
picture another time...

136
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:39,745
- Hey!
- You heartless bitch!

137
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:42,081
You wouldn't let your own kid
have a single grain of salt...

138
00:09:42,164 --> 00:09:44,292
- Oh...
- And yet here you are...

139
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:47,003
sitting here chugging ramen broth!

140
00:09:47,086 --> 00:09:48,588
Ma'am, please...

141
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:50,089
P-please calm down. Calm down.

142
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:51,090
- Please, calm down...
- Who are you?

143
00:09:51,173 --> 00:09:52,216
- What?
- Are you her husband?

144
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,593
No, I'm her d-driver.

145
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:54,635
You're just like him!

146
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:55,845
No! I'm not! I'm not!

147
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:57,722
- Huh?
- She means no harm.

148
00:09:57,805 --> 00:09:59,098
No harm? She seemed pretty malicious to me.

149
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:00,683
No, that's not true.

150
00:10:10,943 --> 00:10:12,737
What on earth is going on?

151
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:15,656
I told you the ratings would be
good, didn't I?

152
00:10:16,365 --> 00:10:18,743
You need real acting chops
to get into this kind of

153
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:20,786
mess.

154
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:22,872
Oh Young-ran.

155
00:10:22,955 --> 00:10:24,665
I'm not dead yet.

156
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:29,253
What? I'm going to die?

157
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:30,796
Just like that?

158
00:10:32,089 --> 00:10:34,133
Assistant director, I...

159
00:10:34,216 --> 00:10:36,302
I died in another drama today, too.

160
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:38,512
The writer had planned
from the very beginning

161
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:40,139
to kill you off.

162
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:41,932
I think

163
00:10:42,016 --> 00:10:44,769
the viewers' complaints were so intense,
the writer may have changed the story.

164
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:46,479
I don't know. I don't know.

165
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:47,730
I...

166
00:10:47,813 --> 00:10:49,607
don't want to live so
badly that I'd have to beg.

167
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:51,567
Fine! Tell them to do whatever they want!

168
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:58,741
Did I yell too much again?

169
00:11:07,792 --> 00:11:08,626
Son.

170
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:10,961
Did you just get back from night practice?

171
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:12,380
I was practicing my shots.

172
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:14,799
Aren't you a defender?

173
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:16,217
Mom.

174
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:18,344
These days, defenders score goals too.

175
00:11:18,427 --> 00:11:21,305
I love that attitude.

176
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:23,808
When you get a chance,
just take the shot.

177
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:24,975
Got it?

178
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:27,353
People only remember the stars.

179
00:11:27,436 --> 00:11:29,146
When Son Heung-min retires,

180
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:31,482
you have to take his place.

181
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:34,485
But Son Heung-min is a forward.

182
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:37,196
Then, how about...

183
00:11:39,073 --> 00:11:40,241
Kim Min-jae.

184
00:11:42,076 --> 00:11:43,244
But...

185
00:11:43,327 --> 00:11:44,745
Am I really going to Germany by myself?

186
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:46,664
Why would you be alone?

187
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:48,457
Your uncle will be there.

188
00:11:48,541 --> 00:11:51,085
I don't even know much about soccer.

189
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:52,837
Still...

190
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:56,090
Your uncle even ran an amateur soccer club
when he was younger.

191
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:58,968
You'll have plenty to talk about.

192
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:01,387
He can help you settle in over there, too.

193
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:06,183
I heard Son Heung-min's father
moved to Germany and lived with him.

194
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:09,812
Son Heung-min's a forward,
and you're a defender.

195
00:12:09,895 --> 00:12:13,357
Not every parent can do what
Son Heung-min's father did.

196
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:16,068
He made such a fuss about going.
Why's he acting like this now?

197
00:12:16,152 --> 00:12:18,779
I'm worried about leaving you here alone!

198
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:22,366
Why's he worrying about me
like I'm some celebrity...

199
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:23,868
Just focus on your soccer!

200
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:29,457
You're here?

201
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,000
Hi.

202
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:32,877
Good morning!

203
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:33,794
Good mor—

204
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:34,920
- Yes.
- Oh!

205
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:36,547
- Hello, Coach.
- Hello.

206
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:48,893
- Ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

207
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:50,644
The side dishes...

208
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:52,771
Why are they all

209
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:55,816
so bland?

210
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:58,986
I'll sign up for cooking classes tomorrow,
ma'am.

211
00:12:59,069 --> 00:13:01,280
You have one month.

212
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:02,990
Improve your cooking.

213
00:13:03,073 --> 00:13:04,200
Yes, ma'am.

214
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:30,809
Hey! Are you okay?

215
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:34,939
Are you all right?

216
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:49,245
Are you feeling okay?

217
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:51,705
I'm fine.

218
00:13:51,789 --> 00:13:54,375
Maybe it's all that Pilates,

219
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:57,878
but I landed pretty gracefully.

220
00:13:59,004 --> 00:14:00,297
Right.

221
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:04,176
Oh, one more thing.

222
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,679
I'm not sure if I should say this now,

223
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:10,015
but we didn't get your death scene,

224
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:12,560
so for Episode 12,
we'll have you still alive.

225
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:13,477
That's what we're going with.

226
00:14:15,312 --> 00:14:18,232
You should've kept rolling

227
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:21,277
when I fell.

228
00:14:22,444 --> 00:14:25,614
You could've edited it in and used it.

229
00:14:29,743 --> 00:14:31,287
Even when I cough,

230
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:33,205
I go, 'Ow, ow.'

231
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:43,007
Get some rest.

232
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:44,967
Thank you.

233
00:14:58,397 --> 00:14:59,398
Mom.

234
00:15:00,065 --> 00:15:01,442
Yeah?

235
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:03,277
Can I not go to Germany?

236
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:04,820
Son,

237
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:07,615
are you giving up soccer
just because I got hurt?

238
00:15:07,698 --> 00:15:10,367
That weak attitude—you
get it from your dad.

239
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:11,368
No!

240
00:15:12,244 --> 00:15:15,164
What if you get hurt again
while you're home alone?

241
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:18,709
I should stay here with you.

242
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:21,921
Come here.

243
00:15:29,511 --> 00:15:32,598
I'm so touched that you care about me,

244
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:36,060
and I'm grateful,

245
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:39,688
but the truth is,

246
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:43,233
I fell on purpose.

247
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:45,194
- What?
- Mom.

248
00:15:45,277 --> 00:15:47,738
If I die in this drama,

249
00:15:47,821 --> 00:15:49,323
I'll only have one drama left.

250
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:52,117
Son,

251
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:54,662
I can't die just yet.

252
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:55,955
Mom, are you stupid?

253
00:15:56,038 --> 00:15:58,791
A son who gives up studying in Germany

254
00:15:58,874 --> 00:16:00,918
because of his mom is even stupider.

255
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,205
I...

256
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:42,376
You ordered chicken.
Why didn't you say anything?

257
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:45,295
You order food for yourself
when we're not home.

258
00:16:45,379 --> 00:16:47,339
I was home, though.

259
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:48,590
Come on, we're family.

260
00:16:48,674 --> 00:16:51,593
The word for family uses the characters for 'eat' and
'mouth.' We're mouths that eat together, aren't we?

261
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:53,178
Please.

262
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:55,723
Please get married and
start a family of your own.

263
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:58,100
How long are we supposed
to keep raising you?

264
00:16:59,601 --> 00:17:01,103
- Here.
- Thanks.

265
00:17:02,771 --> 00:17:04,898
Just have some breast meat.

266
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:10,362
Have a wing. It'll give you some energy.

267
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:11,864
Sure.

268
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:15,868
- Oh, well, I...
- You're the genius?

269
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:21,665
Huh? Mom!

270
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:25,586
I'm off.

271
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:36,430
- Hong-rae.
- Yes?

272
00:17:36,513 --> 00:17:38,098
- Aren't you going?
- Right, I should go.

273
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:40,434
- Go on.
- Goodbye.

274
00:17:58,744 --> 00:17:59,995
Hong-rae?

275
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:02,623
Y-yes.

276
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,140
Your mother is a regular customer.

277
00:18:21,141 --> 00:18:22,476
I've heard a lot about you.

278
00:18:23,435 --> 00:18:25,854
She says you're cheaper
than hiring a road manager.

279
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:32,236
Ma'am.

280
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:34,571
For the right look and flavor,

281
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:36,698
you need to preserve some texture...

282
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:39,201
Has anyone here never tried dongpo pork?

283
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:42,913
Mom, stop it.

284
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:50,462
Son.

285
00:18:50,546 --> 00:18:51,380
I'm trying to focus.

286
00:18:51,964 --> 00:18:54,133
Sorry I yelled, honey.

287
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:56,093
Mom, pay a little attention to me, too.

288
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:00,931
The facilities inside must be nice.

289
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:03,016
You even got your hair completely dry.

290
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:05,352
I'm just a substitute.

291
00:19:05,435 --> 00:19:07,229
I didn't play a single second.

292
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:10,983
You'll keep it a secret from my
mom, right?

293
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:14,236
What a customer says in a taxi

294
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,864
never gets shared with anyone.

295
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:21,743
When are you leaving to
study soccer in Germany?

296
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:23,787
Germany?

297
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:26,415
The grass in Europe is different.

298
00:19:26,498 --> 00:19:29,418
Maybe you'll finally show
your real talent in Germany.

299
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:34,381
I felt like I was getting in the
way of your work by staying here.

300
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:38,677
I wanted to leave for her sake,
not mine.

301
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:42,306
I'm still just a backup here.

302
00:19:43,056 --> 00:19:44,433
Germany would be even worse.

303
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:47,519
Mom, I'm vegan.

304
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:49,188
I don't eat meat.

305
00:19:50,814 --> 00:19:53,525
You ate meat, son.

306
00:19:53,609 --> 00:19:54,776
Hey, just the other day, we...

307
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,279
I only put it in my mouth and spit it out
to make you happy.

308
00:19:57,362 --> 00:19:59,031
You like beef ribs, Mom.

309
00:19:59,114 --> 00:20:01,283
Son, what are you talking about?

310
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:02,743
Since when are you vegan?

311
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:04,286
That can't be.

312
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:05,287
You!

313
00:20:06,121 --> 00:20:07,122
You're not vegan.

314
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:09,958
If you want everything your way,
you should've raised a doll.

315
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:11,668
Why did you have me?

316
00:20:11,752 --> 00:20:13,295
I'm going vegan!

317
00:20:16,423 --> 00:20:19,259
Have you tried being honest
with your mother?

318
00:20:20,135 --> 00:20:21,053
I did.

319
00:20:22,095 --> 00:20:23,013
Twice.

320
00:20:24,097 --> 00:20:25,557
I asked if I could stay
instead of going to Germany.

321
00:20:27,517 --> 00:20:30,729
I think Mom wanted me to go to Germany
more than I did.

322
00:20:32,689 --> 00:20:35,776
Her work is the most
important thing to her.

323
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,111
I guess she can't see me.

324
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:40,864
Family can be so close

325
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:43,075
that sometimes it's hard
to see them clearly.

326
00:20:47,204 --> 00:20:48,121
Son.

327
00:21:10,143 --> 00:21:11,186
Mom...

328
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:15,065
I'm sorry.

329
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:18,235
Is that really the right line?

330
00:21:18,318 --> 00:21:20,529
No, you're supposed to
pry your son's mouth open

331
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:23,031
and force the meat into it like this.

332
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:24,700
Damn it.

333
00:21:24,783 --> 00:21:25,826
Cut! Cut!

334
00:21:25,909 --> 00:21:27,119
Yes, cut!

335
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:32,624
Do you have a son?

336
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:35,627
I'm the son.

337
00:21:35,711 --> 00:21:39,006
I live with my parents too,

338
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:42,467
so we're in the same position.

339
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:50,892
What's this?

340
00:21:51,727 --> 00:21:52,561
Sweetie.

341
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:56,648
- I'm sorry.
- Director.

342
00:21:56,732 --> 00:21:58,859
I don't think this version
is bad either.

343
00:21:58,942 --> 00:21:59,776
What do you think?

344
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:03,113
Now that we put it together,

345
00:22:03,196 --> 00:22:05,324
the bittersweet feeling isn't bad either.

346
00:22:05,407 --> 00:22:06,241
Yeah.

347
00:22:09,911 --> 00:22:12,914
♪ All the love my mother gave ♪

348
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:16,335
♪ I'm awkward when it comes to love ♪

349
00:22:16,418 --> 00:22:19,588
♪ Is that why? ♪

350
00:22:19,671 --> 00:22:23,008
♪ I always find it hard ♪

351
00:22:23,091 --> 00:22:28,722
♪ Even in the longing
I was afraid to lose ♪

352
00:22:29,556 --> 00:22:34,895
♪ There's a little beauty there ♪

353
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:39,066
♪ I'm happy now ♪

354
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:42,486
♪ And that's why I'm uneasy ♪

355
00:22:42,569 --> 00:22:48,533
♪ The sea is always
calm before the storm ♪

356
00:22:49,117 --> 00:22:54,623
♪ We can't let it catch fire
and burn too fast ♪

357
00:22:55,373 --> 00:23:01,922
♪ I'm rooting for love ♪

358
00:23:02,005 --> 00:23:06,426
♪ Us, while we're young ♪

359
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:13,308
♪ Our rings are hard to see ♪

360
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:17,604
♪ The brilliant light... ♪

361
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:25,737
♪ Is fading away ♪

362
00:23:53,390 --> 00:23:56,017
Oh dear, for a while...

363
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:58,395
I'm too scared to even buy
anything to eat.

364
00:23:59,771 --> 00:24:01,940
This is all such a waste.

365
00:24:07,404 --> 00:24:08,321
Mom.

366
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:10,740
What are you doing?

367
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:13,451
You came out because you smelled it, huh?

368
00:24:13,535 --> 00:24:14,703
Here.

369
00:24:14,786 --> 00:24:16,413
There, all done.

370
00:24:18,248 --> 00:24:19,374
Sit down.

371
00:24:20,834 --> 00:24:22,002
Here.

372
00:24:24,421 --> 00:24:26,214
Have the biggest one.

373
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:27,424
That's it.

374
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:29,134
Like this.

375
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:30,802
Here.

376
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:33,305
Son.

377
00:24:33,972 --> 00:24:35,348
Are you, by any chance...

378
00:24:36,391 --> 00:24:37,851
You're not vegan, are you?

379
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:40,687
Huh? You expect me to run on vegetables?

380
00:24:40,770 --> 00:24:43,023
I was just checking.

381
00:24:43,106 --> 00:24:43,940
Hurry up and eat.

382
00:24:51,448 --> 00:24:53,742
It's so good.

383
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:54,951
Did you play well today?

384
00:24:56,328 --> 00:24:58,663
Yeah, I scored a goal today.

385
00:24:58,747 --> 00:25:00,165
Really?

386
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:05,921
I've always known you were
born to be a striker.

387
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:09,257
What, how...
Can’t you change positions now?

388
00:25:09,341 --> 00:25:12,010
You scored one goal.
Why would you change positions?

389
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:16,556
Son.

390
00:25:17,224 --> 00:25:20,185
Mom has lots of time now.

391
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:21,269
I...

392
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:24,272
I haven't been there for you enough.

393
00:25:24,981 --> 00:25:29,402
From now on, I'll come watch all
your games in person, whenever I can.

394
00:25:31,279 --> 00:25:33,698
Come up with a goal celebration for me.

395
00:25:33,782 --> 00:25:36,201
Come on, I'll take your picture, too.

396
00:25:36,868 --> 00:25:37,911
Come on, come on.

397
00:25:37,994 --> 00:25:41,581
Mom, you don't have to come to every game.

398
00:25:41,665 --> 00:25:43,250
I'm worried about your driving, too.

399
00:25:46,711 --> 00:25:49,297
I only have one drama left to do.

400
00:25:49,381 --> 00:25:50,507
It's not even a big role.

401
00:25:52,884 --> 00:25:55,303
I liked the taxi you called for me today.

402
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:57,722
When I have a game,
call that taxi for me like you did today.

403
00:25:58,723 --> 00:25:59,557
You listened to the music, too?

404
00:25:59,641 --> 00:26:01,893
Yeah, the sound was great, too.

405
00:26:01,977 --> 00:26:05,272
That taxi's hard to book.

406
00:26:05,355 --> 00:26:07,649
I asked that driver to be my road manager

407
00:26:07,732 --> 00:26:10,151
so many times, but...

408
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:11,361
He wouldn't go for it.

409
00:26:11,444 --> 00:26:15,073
Mom, no one's lasted more
than a month as your manager.

410
00:26:15,156 --> 00:26:16,491
I wouldn't do it either.

411
00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:21,830
- Son.
- What?

412
00:26:23,081 --> 00:26:26,251
You don't have to go to
Germany if you don't want to.

413
00:26:27,252 --> 00:26:28,086
Huh?

414
00:26:29,212 --> 00:26:32,674
When you said you wanted to go to Germany,

415
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:36,177
I really wanted to help
you do what you wanted.

416
00:26:37,262 --> 00:26:41,516
But it seemed like you were having
second thoughts because of me,

417
00:26:41,599 --> 00:26:43,560
so I pushed you even harder.

418
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:47,480
Are you sure you're okay
with not going to Germany?

419
00:26:48,064 --> 00:26:49,274
Yeah, of course.

420
00:26:49,357 --> 00:26:50,400
It's your decision.

421
00:26:52,152 --> 00:26:55,405
Having you here with me

422
00:26:55,488 --> 00:26:56,573
would make me happy, too.

423
00:27:00,785 --> 00:27:02,329
Eat some more, sweetheart.

424
00:27:02,412 --> 00:27:03,913
Eat up.

425
00:27:04,622 --> 00:27:06,624
You should eat, too, Mom.

426
00:27:06,708 --> 00:27:09,502
I'm in heaven after
eating Dongpo pork today.

427
00:27:12,839 --> 00:27:16,551
'B Side'

428
00:27:16,634 --> 00:27:17,927
Really?

429
00:27:18,011 --> 00:27:20,138
Yeah, I decided not to go to Germany.

430
00:27:20,221 --> 00:27:21,348
What a relief.

431
00:27:21,431 --> 00:27:24,059
I almost sent you all the way to
Germany by yourself, Hong-rae.

432
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:26,186
I didn't even look into it properly,

433
00:27:26,269 --> 00:27:28,730
and I blurted out that I
was leaving for Germany.

434
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:31,900
I heard Dad was being
sent to Germany for work,

435
00:27:31,983 --> 00:27:34,361
so I thought the whole family was going.

436
00:27:34,444 --> 00:27:35,528
Sera.

437
00:27:36,404 --> 00:27:37,822
This whole thing made me realize

438
00:27:37,906 --> 00:27:40,742
and I'm glad we confirmed
that we can never be apart.

439
00:27:42,827 --> 00:27:45,789
No matter where you are,

440
00:27:45,872 --> 00:27:47,457
I'll always be by your side.

441
00:27:47,540 --> 00:27:48,708
Hong-rae.

442
00:27:53,129 --> 00:27:53,963
Just a second.

443
00:27:58,885 --> 00:27:59,719
Yeah, Mom.

444
00:28:03,431 --> 00:28:05,058
Yeah, I'm at night practice.

445
00:28:07,852 --> 00:28:09,229
Mom.

446
00:28:09,312 --> 00:28:11,898
I'm not the kind of player
who fixates on scoring goals.

447
00:28:15,693 --> 00:28:16,528
Okay.

448
00:28:17,779 --> 00:28:18,738
I'll be right there.

449
00:28:27,664 --> 00:28:28,581
Shall we eat?

450
00:28:32,168 --> 00:28:33,044
'Ah.'

451
00:28:51,855 --> 00:28:56,276
♪ We were young ♪

452
00:28:56,359 --> 00:29:03,283
♪ Our growth rings were hard to see ♪

453
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:11,708
♪ Blinded by a dazzling light ♪

454
00:29:11,791 --> 00:29:17,797
♪ We were fading away ♪

455
00:29:17,881 --> 00:29:24,220
♪ Ah-ah-ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah-ah-ah ♪

456
00:29:24,304 --> 00:29:30,727
♪ Ah-ah-ah-ah-ah, ah-ah ♪

457
00:29:30,810 --> 00:29:37,192
♪ Ah-ah-ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah-ah-ah ♪

458
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:43,656
♪ Ah-ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah-ah-ah ♪

459
00:29:43,740 --> 00:29:50,038
♪ Sad adults are always backing away ♪

460
00:29:50,121 --> 00:29:55,877
♪ Past that wretched age of twenty,
you look so bored ♪

461
00:29:56,753 --> 00:30:02,967
♪ We can't let our love catch fire
and burn out too fast ♪

462
00:30:03,051 --> 00:30:09,599
♪ Here's to our love ♪

463
00:30:09,682 --> 00:30:14,103
♪ We were young ♪

464
00:30:14,187 --> 00:30:21,152
♪ Our growth rings were hard to see ♪

465
00:30:22,695 --> 00:30:29,494
♪ Blinded by a dazzling light ♪

466
00:30:29,577 --> 00:30:35,667
♪ We were fading away ♪

467
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:38,419
♪ Yes, back then ♪

468
00:30:38,503 --> 00:30:41,714
♪ I didn't really know ♪

469
00:30:41,798 --> 00:30:45,969
♪ We were alike only in
how we were different ♪

470
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:54,602
♪ You grew up and drifted away first ♪

471
00:30:54,686 --> 00:31:00,024
♪ Now I've become like you ♪

472
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:05,989
♪ We were young ♪

473
00:31:06,072 --> 00:31:13,037
♪ Our growth rings were hard to see ♪

474
00:31:14,581 --> 00:31:21,379
♪ Blinded by a dazzling light ♪

475
00:31:21,462 --> 00:31:27,510
♪ We were fading away ♪

476
00:31:27,594 --> 00:31:34,017
♪ Ah-ah-ah-ah-ah, ah-ah-ah-ah-ah ♪

477
00:31:34,100 --> 00:31:35,310
♪ Ah-ah-ah… ♪
